winless NEWS -- history of user-visible changes

* Version 0.2.0
  (This program was called winview until 2026-11-03; it is now winless -- "less" in its own Windows window.
  Renamed: the command, man page, WINVIEW_* environment variables (now WINLESS_*), and ~/.cache/winview (now
  ~/.cache/winless).)
  Rewritten in C (the 0.1.0 Python server and CLI are gone; viewer.html is unchanged apart from a page-up fix). One
  single-threaded poll() server, no dependencies beyond libc, builds with autoconf. Disconnected windows are noticed
  at once. The window opens full screen by default (--windowed for a normal one); it uses its own browser profile so that Edge
  honours the full-screen flag even when it is already running. Page up now exactly undoes page down.
  The tests are C programs in tests/ (unit tests of the parser and UTF-8 code, plus black-box tests that start the real
  binary); `make check` runs them, `make check-asan` runs them under AddressSanitizer/UBSan. No Python anywhere.

* Version 0.1.0
  First release (Python): a less-style viewer in its own Windows window (chromeless Edge/Chrome app window) driven from
  the shell through a local HTTP/SSE server.
